    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "After a storm damages your roof, ensure personal safety first by staying off the slippery roof, check your home interior for leaks, photograph all visible damage from the ground, apply a temporary tarp if there is an active leak, and call a trusted local roofing contractor for a professional inspection before filing an insurance claim.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "staying off the slippery roof, check your home interior for leaks, photograph all visible damage from the ground, apply a temporary tarp if there is an active leak, and call a trusted local roofing contractor for a professional inspection before filing an insurance claim"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Safety and Ground Inspection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Do not climb onto a wet, high-pitched, or debris-covered roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect from the ground:\nUse binoculars or a phone camera to check for missing shingles, bent gutters, or fallen tree limbs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check the interior: Look at top-floor ceilings and attic spaces for water stains, bulges, or active dripping."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Watch electrical hazards:\nTurn off your main breaker if water is leaking near light fixtures or electrical wiring."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Watch this visual guide on how to safely examine your roof and property from the ground after severe weather:",
        "video": {
          "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bBFCExBd2aw&t=21",
          "thumbnail": "https://serpapi.com/images/i/R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAP_______yH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw.gif"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Documentation and Temporary Protection"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Photograph everything: Capture clear photos and videos of fallen branches, damaged siding, missing shingles, and granule accumulation in your gutters.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Record the event: Note the exact date, time, and severity of the storm for your insurance provider."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Install a temporary tarp: If water is actively leaking inside, secure a heavy-duty waterproof tarp over the damaged area using the \"board sandwich\" method (fastening the tarp edges between wooden 2x4 boards) to prevent further interior ruin."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Professional Assessment and Insurance"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule a professional inspection: Contact a reputable local roofing company to perform a detailed assessment of hidden bruises, shingle cracks, and structural compromises."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File your claim promptly: Provide your contractor\u2019s documented findings and your photo logs to your homeowners insurance company within their required filing window."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid aggressive door-to-door contractors: Decline high-pressure offers from transient \"storm-chasing\" roofers who show up uninvited after severe weather."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What kind of visible damage\nyou see from the ground (missing shingles, tree limb impact, leaks)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are expecting more rain or storms in your area soon"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prioritize your next steps or advise on emergency fixes."
      }
    ],
